&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Welcome to Planet. We believe in using space to help life on Earth.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Planet designs, builds, and operates the largest constellation of imaging satellites in history. This constellation delivers an unprecedented dataset of empirical information via a revolutionary cloud-based platform to authoritative figures in commercial, environmental, and humanitarian sectors. We are both a space company and data company all rolled into one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Customers and users across the globe use Planet&#39;s data to develop new technologies, drive revenue, power research, and solve our world’s toughest obstacles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As we control every component of hardware design, manufacturing, data processing, and software engineering, our office is a truly inspiring mix of experts from a variety of domains.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a people-centric approach toward culture and community and we strive to iterate in a way that puts our team members first and prepares our company for growth. Join Planet and be a part of our mission to change the way people see the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Planet is a global company with employees working remotely world wide and joining us from offices in San Francisco, Washington DC, Germany, Austria, Slovenia, and The Netherlands.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Director of Pre-Sales, Global Defence &amp;amp; Intelligence (D&amp;amp;I)&lt;/strong&gt; will be responsible for leading Pre-Sales Solution Architects worldwide. This leader will deliver excellence in technical sales, account strategy, relationship building, and solution architecting tailored specifically to national security, Defence &amp;amp; Intelligence institutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The mission of Pre-Sales is to provide trusted technical advice, enabling global defence customers to leverage Earth Observation data and geospatial intelligence to support critical military operations, decision-making, and strategic outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is an accomplished people manager, a geospatial expert with strong commercial acumen, and possesses over 10 years of experience in Defence &amp;amp; Intelligence. You possess a deep understanding of government defense customers, complex procurement frameworks, and military command structures.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a visible, strategic, and highly influential global role, partnering closely with internal D&amp;amp;I Sales teams, Space Systems, Product Engineering, and trusted defense partner ecosystems to secure complex, large-scale government contracts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full-time, remote position based in the UK or Germany. If located near an office, you are expected to work from that office 3 days per week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Impact You’ll Own:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create the conditions for high performance; recruit, coach, and develop a global team of specialized D&amp;amp;I Pre-Sales Solution Architects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support global D&amp;amp;I sales teams and partner ecosystems by providing world-class technical sales capability to win new defense programs and expand existing accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply deep expertise in remote sensing, imagery analytics, and complex data architecture to design solutions supporting Military Operations, Intelligence, Surveillance, and Reconnaissance (ISR) workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead high-impact customer engagements, workshops, pilots, and technical demonstrations tailored to defense commanders, intelligence analysts, and procurement officers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Global Professional Services, Program Management and Customer Success to conduct rigorous technical assessments, ensuring flawless execution from validation to operational delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feed insights, security requirements, and intelligence use cases directly back to Product and Marketing to shape the product roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a core member of the Global Pre-Sales &amp;amp; Services leadership team, shaping overarching department strategy and driving execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of relevant work experience and 6+ years of supervisory or leadership experience managing and scaling technical sales (Pre-Sales / Solution Architecture) teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of professional experience in a Defence &amp;amp; Intelligence environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active Security Clearance (or eligibility to hold suitable clearance for engaging all levels of Military Command).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid grasp of military planning, intelligence workflows, and how commercial Earth Observation (EO) data integrates into defense decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience navigating complex government sales cycles, RFP/RFI processes, and defense contracting frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in geospatial system architectures, cloud environments/secure deployments, API integrations, and complex data pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to engage senior defense executives, military leaders, and procurement authorities, translating technical complexity into strategic value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, organizational, and leadership skills with a track record of building resilient, high-trust teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Makes You Stand Out:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Military / Veteran Experience: Former active Armed Forces Reserve or veteran intelligence professional.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with Sales Qualification frameworks and methodologies e.g., Challenger Sales, MEDDPICC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of AI-Driven Geospatial Innovation: Conversant in modern AI/ML capabilities (e.g., automated feature extraction, change detection, foundation models) and skilled at leveraging AI to demonstrate high-value intelligence outcomes to defense customers—moving beyond raw imagery to automated, actionable insights.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience co-selling and architecting solutions alongside major defense prime contractors, system integrators, and international allies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application Deadline:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;November 30, 2026 at 11:59p PT&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits While Working at Planet:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;These offerings are dependent on employment type and geographical location, based upon applicable law or company policy.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid time off including vacation, holidays and company-wide days off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Wellness Program&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Home Office Reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly Phone and Internet Reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition Reimbursement and access to LinkedIn Learning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Volunteering Paid Time Off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected starting gross salary range for this role is listed below. Individual placement within this range is determined objectively based on gender-neutral criteria such as your skills, qualifications, and professional experience. This position may also be eligible for discretionary bonuses, commission, and/or equity.&lt;/p&gt;
